## Context

First child of 0700. Nothing gets drafted until the expected form is known and
the outline is settled: a four-month literature review that discovers its
format constraints at the end has to be redone.

## Actions

1. Retrieve the author guidelines of *Reviews of Economic Literature*:
   length, reference format and style, preprint policy, licence, figures and
   tables, expected structure of a review. Store them in
   `~/CNRS/papiers/actif/REL_Climate_Finance_Literature_Review/instructions to authors/`,
   as done for *Oeconomia — Joint production*.
2. Create the workpackage `deliverables/literature-review/` modelled on its
   neighbours (`_quarto.yml`, `<name>-vars.yml`, `<name>.mk`, `<name>.qmd`),
   wired to `deliverables/_shared/`.
3. Write the detailed outline: the two moves of the proposal (bibliometrics,
   then narrative synthesis), the place of the section on the four accounting
   controversies, and the word allocation.
4. Have the author validate the outline before any drafting.

## Invariants

- The scope is an agreement with an editor: the outline instantiates it, it
  does not widen it. Any deviation is rediscussed with the editorial side.
- The workpackage is built from the repository's artifacts, with no data access
  at drafting time (workpackage separation discipline).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Author guidelines retrieved and archived
- [ ] `deliverables/literature-review/` built and rendering an empty but valid PDF
- [ ] Detailed outline written and validated by the author
